 <h2>Common questions</h2>
 <details><summary>Should I take creatine on semaglutide or tirzepatide?</summary><p>No trial answers this directly. Creatine adds lean tissue when combined with resistance training in older adults, so it is a reasonable question to raise with your clinician if you are doing strength training. It is not a substitute for training or adequate protein.</p></details>
 <details><summary>How much of the weight lost on GLP-1 drugs is muscle?</summary><p>In trials that measured it, roughly a quarter of weight lost came from lean mass, with wide variation between studies. In SURMOUNT-1 the proportion was the same for tirzepatide and placebo.</p></details>
 <details><summary>Which magnesium is used for constipation?</summary><p>The trial evidence and the gastroenterology guideline are for magnesium oxide. People with kidney disease should ask a clinician first.</p></details>
 <details><summary>Does biotin stop hair loss on Ozempic or Wegovy?</summary><p>There is no evidence that it does. Published benefit from biotin is limited to people with a deficiency or an underlying condition.</p></details>
 <details><summary>Can I take berberine with a GLP-1 drug?</summary><p>The combination has not been tested in a trial. Both lower blood sugar, so check with your prescriber first.</p></details>
 
 <h2>How this page was put together</h2>
 <p>Trial figures come from the published abstracts and from the FDA-approved Wegovy label. Statements that we "found no trial" reflect PubMed searches run on November 10, 2026; they mean no study turned up, not that one cannot exist. Supplement Intelligence may earn referral credit from some product links elsewhere on this site. No products are recommended on this page.</p>
 
